{
  "name": "Records Store (Google Sheets)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Keep website records in a Google Sheet\n\nOne small store that other workflows call to keep, read and drop rows. This one keeps each table as a tab of one spreadsheet.\n\n### How it works\n**Three operations, one contract.** `keep` adds a row, or writes its fields over the row whose `key` field has the same value. `read` returns one item per row. `drop` removes rows added before a time; a row with a key has no age and stays.\n\n**The header row decides the columns.** A field is written under the column of the same name. A field with no column stops the run, so nothing is dropped quietly. The store stamps the `at` column itself.\n\nRows are appended through the Sheets API, which does not lose rows when two arrive together.\n\n### Setup steps\n1. Bind your **Google Sheets** credential on the four request nodes.\n2. In **Set Store Config**, set `spreadsheet_id`.\n3. Give each table a tab of the same name. Row 1 holds `at` and one column per field.\n4. Activate, then select this workflow in each caller's store node.",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 480
      },
      "id": "c9e3a4f2-18a1-4c00-9a01-000000000001",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Read the tab, then act on it\n\nKeep reads only the header unless it must find a key.",
        "height": 680,
